# Caches — all regenerable, none of it source.
#
# charts/     NOAA ENC raster tiles. Grows to gigabytes on a localized area, and the
#             app reads through to the ASV console's copy anyway.
# ofs_cache/  Downloaded current forecasts (~19 MB for this line, more for others).
#             A cycle is stale within hours; committing one would pin the repo to a
#             particular afternoon's tide and be wrong by the time anyone cloned it.
#             domains.json lives here too — a probe cache, rebuilt in ~4 seconds.
charts/
ofs_cache/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Atomic-write temporaries (tile fetch, domain cache)
*.part
*.part.*

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Desktop shortcut: a binary carrying absolute paths for ONE machine.
# tools/make_shortcut.ps1 rebuilds it anywhere.
*.lnk

# Rasterised document pages: a VERIFICATION artifact, regenerated on demand by
# tools/render_docs.py. The .docx and .pdf in docs/ are the deliverables.
tools/pages/

# Saved missions: working outputs that accumulate, not source. The manuals in
# docs/ ARE tracked; these are not.
docs/missions/
